1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--transcription","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/transcription","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/transcription","sourceHash":"5f50a0cfd152af930f453b93422abee7e76030481f28256be501ed45e7fa347e","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:19.101Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Transcription","zh":"听写"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Transcription means listening to audio in the target language and writing down exactly what you hear, word for word. Then (ideally) checking your work against a transcript or with a native speaker.","zh":"听写是指聆听目标语言的音频，并逐字逐句准确写下你听到的内容。之后（最好）再对照文字稿检查，或请母语者帮你检查。"}},{"id":"how-to-do-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Do It","zh":"操作方法"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Load an audio clip (podcast, YouTube video, audiobook)","zh":"加载一段音频（播客、YouTube视频或有声书）"},{"en":"Listen to a short section (5-15 seconds) a few times","zh":"选择一小段内容（5—15秒），反复听几遍"},{"en":"Write down everything you hear, as accurately as you can","zh":"尽可能准确地写下你听到的一切"},{"en":"If you're not sure about a word, make your best guess based on the sounds","zh":"如果不确定某个词，根据听到的声音尽量猜测"},{"en":"Check your transcription against the official text (subtitles, transcript, or have a native check it)","zh":"将听写内容与官方文本核对（字幕、文字稿，或请母语者检查）"},{"en":"Pay attention to what you missed — were there sounds you didn't hear? Words that blended together?","zh":"注意自己遗漏的内容——有没有没听见的声音？有没有连在一起的词？"},{"en":"Relisten to the section, focusing on the parts you missed","zh":"重新聆听这段内容，重点关注遗漏的部分"},{"en":"Move on to a new section","zh":"继续练习新的片段"}]},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Increase the length of the sections as you build confidence and comfort.","zh":"随着信心和熟练度的提升，逐渐延长每个片段的时长。"}},{"id":"why-its-so-effective","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It's So Effective","zh":"为什么如此有效"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Transcription forces you to hear <em>every single word</em>. During normal listening, your brain fills in gaps and glosses over unfamiliar sounds. Transcription strips that away — you either heard the word or you didn't.","zh":"听写会迫使你听清<em>每一个词</em>。正常聆听时，你的大脑会自动填补空白，并忽略不熟悉的声音。听写会剥去这一层保护——你要么听到了这个词，要么没有听到。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It's brutally revealing. You'll discover sounds you've been mishearing, words that run together in ways you didn't expect, and patterns you've been ignoring. This makes it one of the most powerful exercises for improving listening accuracy.","zh":"它会无情地揭示问题。你会发现自己一直听错的声音、以出乎意料的方式连读在一起的词，以及一直忽略的模式。这使它成为提升听力准确度最有力的练习之一。"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"提示"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Start with short sections and gradually increase length","zh":"从较短的片段开始，逐渐增加长度"},{"en":"Use content at an appropriate level — not so hard that you can't transcribe anything","zh":"使用难度适当的内容——不要难到让你几乎什么都听写不出来"},{"en":"An audio tool like Audacity helps you select and repeat specific sections","zh":"Audacity等音频工具可以帮助你选择并重复特定片段"},{"en":"Official transcriptions sometimes differ from what was actually said (spoken language isn't always grammatically perfect). Trust your ears.","zh":"官方听写稿有时会与实际说出的内容不同（口语并不总是语法完美）。相信自己的耳朵。"},{"en":"This is hard, especially at first. You'll improve with practice.","zh":"这项练习很难，尤其是在刚开始时。但通过练习，你会逐渐进步。"},{"en":"If you struggle to do transcription due to tool setup, you might benefit from transcription cards:","zh":"如果因为工具设置而难以进行听写，你可能会受益于听写卡片："}]},{"id":"when-to-use-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Use It","zh":"何时使用"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Transcription is introduced in Phase 3C as a core listening exercise and remains useful through Phase 6.","zh":"听写在阶段3C作为核心听力练习引入，并在阶段6之前一直都很有用。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
